# Per-Dockerfile BuildKit ignore for docker/Dockerfile.xe-node.
# BuildKit auto-loads "<dockerfile>.dockerignore" in preference to a root
# .dockerignore. Patterns are matched against the BUILD CONTEXT ROOT, which for
# this image is the PARENT C0re repo root (see header of Dockerfile.xe-node).
#
# WARNING: the include-only strategy below ("*" then "!<path>") REQUIRES BuildKit.
# The classic builder does not support negation of a wildcard-all rule and will
# send an EMPTY context, causing the build to fail silently. Always build with
# DOCKER_BUILDKIT=1 (or Docker Engine >= 23 where BuildKit is the default).
#
# Strategy: ignore everything at the context root, then re-include ONLY the
# paths the Dockerfile COPYs. This keeps the context upload to ~tens of MB
# instead of the multi-GB parent tree (.opencode/.cache alone is ~1 GB).

# --- ignore the whole tree ---
*

# --- re-include exactly what the Dockerfile needs ---
!Directory.Build.props
!Directory.Packages.props
!Apps/XE-Local-AI-Engine

# --- prune build output / tooling junk inside the re-included paths ---
**/bin
**/obj
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.git
**/.vs
**/.tmp
**/.opencode
**/.codegraph
**/.omc
**/.idea
**/.vscode
**/TestResults
**/*.user
**/.DS_Store
